POLICY §PERF-EVIDENCE-PREVIEW (ADR-250, 2026-08-04):

1. `useAllKpis` MUST read via `public.get_all_kpis_slim()` (STABLE SECURITY DEFINER) paged with `fetchAllRpcPaged`. Never reintroduce `supabase.from('kpis').select(SLIM_KPI_SELECT)` over the whole table — it was 267k calls / 591ms mean / 7.95s max against an 8s statement_timeout and starved the Storage API.
2. `EvidencePreviewDialog` resolves a 10-min signed URL and streams; `storage.download()` blob-buffering is forbidden. 20s timeout (`PREVIEW_TIMEOUT_MS`) + Retry button required.
3. `normalizeEvidenceError` classifies timeout/abort/5xx/429 as "server busy" (`EVIDENCE_SERVER_BUSY_MESSAGE`); only 403/404/RLS render access-denied.
4. `review-evidence` storage SELECT policies call `public.can_read_kpi_evidence(uuid)` which uses `(select auth.uid())` for per-statement caching.

Guards: `src/test/allKpisRpcContract.test.ts`, `src/test/evidenceErrorTransient.test.ts`.

## Failure clarity (ADR-298, POLICY §EVIDENCE-PREVIEW-FAILURE-CLARITY)

`normalizeEvidenceError` has THREE outcomes, not two:
- `isNetworkBlockedEvidenceError` (status-less `Failed to fetch` / NetworkError / Load failed / net::ERR_*) → `EVIDENCE_NETWORK_BLOCKED_MESSAGE` — not retryable, blame the extension/ad-blocker/proxy.
- `isTransientEvidenceError` (5xx/408/429/57014/timeout, server answered) → `EVIDENCE_SERVER_BUSY_MESSAGE` — retryable.
- 403/404/RLS → `EVIDENCE_ACCESS_DENIED_MESSAGE`.

Signing retries with backoff `[400, 1200]ms` inside the 20s guard and short-circuits on network-blocked. Error state must show the copyable `describeEvidenceFailure()` diagnostics line.
